---@field serviceAddressCidrBlocks? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringList Required. All services in the cluster are assigned an RFC1918 IPv4 address from these ranges. This field is mutable after creation starting with version 1.15.

---KubeletConfig defines the modifiable kubelet configurations for bare metal machines. Note: this list includes fields supported in GKE (see https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/node-system-config#kubelet-options).
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalKubeletConfig
---@field registryPullQps? number The limit of registry pulls per second. Setting this value to 0 means no limit. Updating this field may impact scalability by changing the amount of traffic produced by image pulls. Defaults to 5.
---@field serializeImagePullsDisabled? boolean Prevents the Kubelet from pulling multiple images at a time. We recommend *not* changing the default value on nodes that run docker daemon with version < 1.9 or an Another Union File System (Aufs) storage backend. Issue https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/10959 has more details.
---@field registryBurst? number The maximum size of bursty pulls, temporarily allows pulls to burst to this number, while still not exceeding registry_pull_qps. The value must not be a negative number. Updating this field may impact scalability by changing the amount of traffic produced by image pulls. Defaults to 10.

---Represents an IP pool used by the load balancer.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerAddressPool
---@field addresses? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringList Required. The addresses that are part of this pool. Each address must be either in the CIDR form (1.2.3.0/24) or range form (1.2.3.1-1.2.3.5).
---@field avoidBuggyIps? boolean If true, avoid using IPs ending in .0 or .255. This avoids buggy consumer devices mistakenly dropping IPv4 traffic for those special IP addresses.
---@field manualAssign? boolean If true, prevent IP addresses from being automatically assigned.
---@field pool? string Required. The name of the address pool.

---@alias gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerAddressPoolList gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerAddressPool[]

---Specifies the load balancer configuration.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerConfig
---@field vipConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalVipConfig The VIPs used by the load balancer.
---@field manualLbConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalManualLbConfig Manually configured load balancers.
---@field metalLbConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMetalLbConfig Configuration for MetalLB load balancers.
---@field portConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalPortConfig Configures the ports that the load balancer will listen on.
---@field bgpLbConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalBgpLbConfig Configuration for BGP typed load balancers. When set network_config.advanced_networking is automatically set to true.

---Specifies the load balancer's node pool configuration.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerNodePoolConfig
---@field nodePoolConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePoolConfig The generic configuration for a node pool running a load balancer.

---Specifies the configs for local persistent volumes (PVs).
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLvpConfig
---@field storageClass? string Required. The StorageClass name that PVs will be created with.
---@field path? string Required. The host machine path.

---Specifies the configs for local persistent volumes under a shared file system.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLvpShareConfig
---@field lvpConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLvpConfig Required. Defines the machine path and storage class for the LVP Share.
---@field sharedPathPvCount? number The number of subdirectories to create under path.

---Represents the status of node machines that are undergoing drain operations.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMachineDrainStatus
---@field drainingMachines? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalDrainingMachineList The list of draning machines.
---@field drainedMachines? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalDrainedMachineList The list of drained machines.

---Specifies configurations to put bare metal nodes in and out of maintenance.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMaintenanceConfig
---@field maintenanceAddressCidrBlocks? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringList Required. All IPv4 address from these ranges will be placed into maintenance mode. Nodes in maintenance mode will be cordoned and drained. When both of these are true, the "baremetal.cluster.gke.io/maintenance" annotation will be set on the node resource.

---Represents the maintenance status of the bare metal user cluster.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMaintenanceStatus
---@field machineDrainStatus? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMachineDrainStatus The maintenance status of node machines.

---Represents configuration parameters for a manual load balancer.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalManualLbConfig
---@field enabled? boolean Whether manual load balancing is enabled.

---Represents configuration parameters for a MetalLB load balancer.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMetalLbConfig
---@field addressPools? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerAddressPoolList Required. AddressPools is a list of non-overlapping IP pools used by load balancer typed services. All addresses must be routable to load balancer nodes. IngressVIP must be included in the pools.
---@field loadBalancerNodePoolConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalLoadBalancerNodePoolConfig Specifies the node pool running the load balancer. L2 connectivity is required among nodes in this pool. If missing, the control plane node pool is used as the load balancer pool.

---Specifies the multiple networking interfaces cluster configuration.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMultipleNetworkInterfacesConfig
---@field enabled? boolean Whether to enable multiple network interfaces for your pods. When set network_config.advanced_networking is automatically set to true.

---Specifies the cluster network configuration.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNetworkConfig
---@field advancedNetworking? boolean Enables the use of advanced Anthos networking features, such as Bundled Load Balancing with BGP or the egress NAT gateway. Setting configuration for advanced networking features will automatically set this flag.
---@field islandModeCidr? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalIslandModeCidrConfig Configuration for island mode CIDR. In an island-mode network, nodes have unique IP addresses, but pods don't have unique addresses across clusters. This doesn't cause problems because pods in one cluster never directly communicate with pods in another cluster. Instead, there are gateways that mediate between a pod in one cluster and a pod in another cluster.
---@field multipleNetworkInterfacesConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalMultipleNetworkInterfacesConfig Configuration for multiple network interfaces.
---@field srIovConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalSrIovConfig Configuration for SR-IOV.

---Specifies the node access related settings for the bare metal user cluster.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodeAccessConfig
---@field loginUser? string LoginUser is the user name used to access node machines. It defaults to "root" if not set.

---BareMetalNodeConfig lists machine addresses to access Nodes.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodeConfig
---@field nodeIp? string The default IPv4 address for SSH access and Kubernetes node. Example: 192.168.0.1
---@field labels? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringMap The labels assigned to this node. An object containing a list of key/value pairs. The labels here, unioned with the labels set on BareMetalNodePoolConfig are the set of labels that will be applied to the node. If there are any conflicts, the BareMetalNodeConfig labels take precedence. Example: { "name": "wrench", "mass": "1.3kg", "count": "3" }.

---@alias gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodeConfigList gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodeConfig[]

---Resource that represents a bare metal node pool.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePool
---@field nodePoolConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePoolConfig Required. Node pool configuration.
---@field uid? string Output only. The unique identifier of the bare metal node pool.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time at which this bare metal node pool was last updated.
---@field name? string Immutable. The bare metal node pool resource name.
---@field displayName? string The display name for the bare metal node pool.
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. The time at which this bare metal node pool was deleted. If the resource is not deleted, this must be empty
---@field state? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePoolStateEnum Output only. The current state of the bare metal node pool.
---@field upgradePolicy? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePoolUpgradePolicy The worker node pool upgrade policy.
---@field etag? string This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of other fields, and may be sent on update and delete requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding. Allows clients to perform consistent read-modify-writes through optimistic concurrency control.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time at which this bare metal node pool was created.
---@field status? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.ResourceStatus Output only. ResourceStatus representing the detailed node pool status.
---@field reconciling? boolean Output only. If set, there are currently changes in flight to the bare metal node pool.
---@field annotations? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringMap Annotations on the bare metal node pool. This field has the same restrictions as Kubernetes annotations. The total size of all keys and values combined is limited to 256k. Key can have 2 segments: prefix (optional) and name (required), separated by a slash (/). Prefix must be a DNS subdomain. Name must be 63 characters or less, begin and end with alphanumerics, with dashes (-), underscores (_), dots (.), and alphanumerics between.

---BareMetalNodePoolConfig describes the configuration of all nodes within a given bare metal node pool.
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePoolConfig
---@field kubeletConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalKubeletConfig The modifiable kubelet configurations for the bare metal machines.
---@field taints? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.NodeTaintList The initial taints assigned to nodes of this node pool.
---@field operatingSystem? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodePoolConfigOperatingSystemEnum|string Specifies the nodes operating system (default: LINUX).
---@field nodeConfigs? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BareMetalNodeConfigList Required. The list of machine addresses in the bare metal node pool.
---@field labels? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringMap The labels assigned to nodes of this node pool. An object containing a list of key/value pairs. Example: { "name": "wrench", "mass": "1.3kg", "count": "3" }.

