---Resource that represents a VMware user cluster. ##
---@class gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareCluster
---@field etag? string This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of other fields, and may be sent on update and delete requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding. Allows clients to perform consistent read-modify-writes through optimistic concurrency control.
---@field autoRepairConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareAutoRepairConfig Configuration for auto repairing.
---@field onPremVersion? string Required. The Anthos clusters on the VMware version for your user cluster.
---@field storage? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareStorageConfig Storage configuration.
---@field fleet? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.Fleet Output only. Fleet configuration for the cluster.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time at which VMware user cluster was created.
---@field controlPlaneNode? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareControlPlaneNodeConfig VMware user cluster control plane nodes must have either 1 or 3 replicas.
---@field loadBalancer? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareLoadBalancerConfig Load balancer configuration.
---@field vcenter? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareVCenterConfig VmwareVCenterConfig specifies vCenter config for the user cluster. If unspecified, it is inherited from the admin cluster.
---@field validationCheck? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.ValidationCheck Output only. ValidationCheck represents the result of the preflight check job.
---@field upgradePolicy? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareClusterUpgradePolicy Specifies upgrade policy for the cluster.
---@field state? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareClusterStateEnum Output only. The current state of VMware user cluster.
---@field antiAffinityGroups? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareAAGConfig AAGConfig specifies whether to spread VMware user cluster nodes across at least three physical hosts in the datacenter.
---@field uid? string Output only. The unique identifier of the VMware user cluster.
---@field networkConfig? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareNetworkConfig The VMware user cluster network configuration.
---@field annotations? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.StringMap Annotations on the VMware user cluster. This field has the same restrictions as Kubernetes annotations. The total size of all keys and values combined is limited to 256k. Key can have 2 segments: prefix (optional) and name (required), separated by a slash (/). Prefix must be a DNS subdomain. Name must be 63 characters or less, begin and end with alphanumerics, with dashes (-), underscores (_), dots (.), and alphanumerics between.
---@field reconciling? boolean Output only. If set, there are currently changes in flight to the VMware user cluster.
---@field localName? string Output only. The object name of the VMware OnPremUserCluster custom resource on the associated admin cluster. This field is used to support conflicting names when enrolling existing clusters to the API. When used as a part of cluster enrollment, this field will differ from the ID in the resource name. For new clusters, this field will match the user provided cluster name and be visible in the last component of the resource name. It is not modifiable. All users should use this name to access their cluster using gkectl or kubectl and should expect to see the local name when viewing admin cluster controller logs.
---@field enableAdvancedCluster? boolean Enable advanced cluster.
---@field vmTrackingEnabled? boolean Enable VM tracking.
---@field authorization? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.Authorization RBAC policy that will be applied and managed by the Anthos On-Prem API.
---@field dataplaneV2? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.VmwareDataplaneV2Config VmwareDataplaneV2Config specifies configuration for Dataplane V2.
---@field binaryAuthorization? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.BinaryAuthorization Binary Authorization related configurations.
---@field adminClusterMembership? string Required. The admin cluster this VMware user cluster belongs to. This is the full resource name of the admin cluster's fleet membership. In the future, references to other resource types might be allowed if admin clusters are modeled as their own resources.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time at which VMware user cluster was last updated.
---@field enableControlPlaneV2? boolean Enable control plane V2. Default to false.
---@field disableBundledIngress? boolean Disable bundled ingress.
---@field name? string Immutable. The VMware user cluster resource name.
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. The time at which VMware user cluster was deleted.
---@field endpoint? string Output only. The DNS name of VMware user cluster's API server.
---@field adminClusterName? string Output only. The resource name of the VMware admin cluster hosting this user cluster.
---@field description? string A human readable description of this VMware user cluster.
---@field status? gcp.gkeonprem_v1.ResourceStatus Output only. ResourceStatus representing detailed cluster state.

